Declare +calendarWithIdentifier:, which has existed since 10.9.

It was neither declared nor implemented, so the documented way to get a calendar for an identifier
took doesNotRecognizeSelector: and an uncaught exception, which exits 0. The implementation goes in
with corefoundation patch 0128; this is the declaration so callers compile against it.

Task #253.

--- a/include/Foundation/NSCalendar.h
+++ b/include/Foundation/NSCalendar.h
@@ -71,6 +71,8 @@
 @interface NSCalendar : NSObject <NSCopying, NSSecureCoding>
 
 + (id)currentCalendar;
+/* 10.9 and later, and the documented way to get a calendar for an identifier. */
++ (id)calendarWithIdentifier:(NSCalendarIdentifier)calendarIdentifierConstant;
 + (id)autoupdatingCurrentCalendar;
 
 - (id)initWithCalendarIdentifier:(NSCalendarIdentifier)ident;
